# Index

Select applicable skills before starting a new substantive task. This catalog is
generated from CLI-managed installations in this scope; it does not list every
plugin or skill installed by other tools. Consider other available skill metadata
when relevant. Installation does not mean every skill body should be loaded.

1. Choose the relevant category below from the requested outcome. Read its pages
   before opening candidate skill instructions. Pages contain at most 2,500
   characters, entry counts, and exact continuation paths. Read further pages as
   needed; a partial page cannot establish that no relevant skill exists.
2. Resolve catalog paths against `metadata.catalog-base` in this file's
   frontmatter, not the agent's symlink or junction directory. Follow those exact
   local paths.
   Read selected SKILL.md files before work: the task workflow plus applicable
   platform or language guidance. Summaries do not replace full instructions.
3. Preserve the requested scope: a review does not authorize fixes, and finding
   a skill does not authorize installing more skills or changing configuration.
4. Reuse instructions within the same task; reconsider selection when scope
   changes. If no applicable installed skill exists, proceed within the user's
   scope and identify any missing required instructions.

## Installed catalog

{{catalog}}

The CLI regenerates this skill after installation changes. Do not edit generated
files; update the source skills or installation selection instead. Verify local
paths if files were changed outside the CLI. Mention selected skills briefly when
useful; do not create a separate selection report for every task.

## Saved records

Save only when requested or needed by this workflow. User/project paths take
precedence; default: `<project-root>/.agents/artifacts/<run-id>/<skill-name>/`.
Use a UTC timestamp plus unique suffix for a new run; reuse an explicitly shared ID.
Add a short `summary.md` linking raw evidence when useful. Preserve existing files
unless updating them was requested. Return exact paths; commit or publish records
only when requested. Disposable command files use OS temp.
